  "title": "Birth of a child",
  "highlighted": false,
  "category": "Family & Children",
  "body": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "value": "<p data-block-key=\"dc0ct\">This page breaks it down into clear steps: before the birth, immediately after giving birth, health and care in the early weeks, employment rights, financial and childcare supports, and other steps you should take.</p>",
      "id": "441fc003-758d-4a45-a102-c696201e40ba"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "value": "Before giving birth",
      "id": "2ede0190-2de5-4de6-ac73-5b54a258dbee"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "value": "<h3 data-block-key=\"dc0ct\">Sort out work leave</h3><p data-block-key=\"72p9\">Confirm maternity, paternity, or parent's leave dates with your employer.</p><p data-block-key=\"a1put\">You are entitled to paid time-off work to attend any medical visits (also known as <a href=\"https://www2.hse.ie/pregnancy-birth/pregnancy-care/care-appointments/\">antenatal visits or appointments</a>) associated with the pregnancy and to attend a certain number of <a href=\"https://www2.hse.ie/pregnancy-birth/pregnancy-care/antenatal-classes/\">antenatal classes</a>.</p><p data-block-key=\"6htpn\">You may be eligible for <a href=\"https://www.gov.ie/en/department-of-social-protection/services/maternity-benefit/\">Maternity Benefit</a> or <a href=\"https://www.gov.ie/en/department-of-social-protection/services/paternity-benefit/\">Paternity Benefit</a> - but this depends on your previous social insurance (PRSI) contributions.</p><h3 data-block-key=\"k285\">Get baby essentials ready at home</h3><p data-block-key=\"1414m\">These include a cot or bassinet, car seat (this is legally required to bring your baby home), clothes, nappies, and feeding supplies.</p><h3 data-block-key=\"60jv5\">Have a hospital bag ready</h3><p data-block-key=\"89v9b\">This should include clothes for you and your baby, nappies, maternity pads, toiletries, hospital notes, and proof of ID.</p><p data-block-key=\"ap283\"><a href=\"https://www2.hse.ie/pregnancy-birth/labour/preparing/hospital-bag/\">Guidance on hospital bags from the HSE</a>.</p><h3 data-block-key=\"8dgp8\">Plan your hospital trip</h3><p data-block-key=\"6alvf\">Decide how you'll get to the hospital, for example, by car or taxi. Make sure you can access transport whenever you'll need it.</p><p data-block-key=\"7krpv\">Save phone numbers for the hospital.</p>",
      "id": "73d73042-5376-47cf-b97a-026e2f6aee2d"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "value": "Immediately after birth",
      "id": "f06c13bf-216f-44d1-96cc-88abe4e54ef0"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "value": "<h3 data-block-key=\"dc0ct\">Register the birth</h3><p data-block-key=\"6766s\">The hospital gives you a Birth Notification Form.</p><p data-block-key=\"6652k\">You should register the birth of your baby within 3 months of their birth. If you meet <a href=\"https://www.gov.ie/en/department-of-social-protection/services/register-a-birth-in-ireland/#how-to-register-a-birth-online\">certain criteria</a>, you can <a href=\"https://civilregistration.mywelfare.ie/\">register the birth online</a>. Otherwise, you should register the birth at <a href=\"https://www2.hse.ie/services/births-deaths-and-marriages/find-a-civil-registration-service/\">your local Civil Registration Service</a>.</p><p data-block-key=\"1b8it\">You should also <a href=\"https://forms.uat.services.gov.ie/en/67dbe89f14f22400128523b2-order-a-birth-certificate\">order copies of the birth certificate</a>.</p><h3 data-block-key=\"ava6r\">Get your baby's PPS Number</h3><p data-block-key=\"b31m8\">This is automatically issued after you register the birth.</p><p data-block-key=\"2j1p\">You'll need this for benefits, health services, and childcare supports.</p><h3 data-block-key=\"eatvi\">Apply for Child Benefit</h3><p data-block-key=\"9qcrr\">This is <a href=\"https://www.gov.ie/en/department-of-social-protection/services/child-benefit/\">a monthly payment of €140 per child</a>.</p><p data-block-key=\"29qjf\">To apply, you'll need your baby's PPS Number.</p>",
      "id": "682c4d30-bf3f-453a-9988-8bc7c9344efd"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "value": "Health and care in the first weeks",
      "id": "f7b5b27e-6ec1-433c-9b91-1805eca1e325"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "value": "<h3 data-block-key=\"dc0ct\">Register with a GP</h3><p data-block-key=\"2b1h2\">Let your GP know about your new baby.</p><p data-block-key=\"ajs33\">Register online for a <a href=\"https://www2.hse.ie/services/schemes-allowances/gp-visit-cards/under-8s/\">GP Visit Card</a>. This covers free GP visits for children under 8 years old.</p><h3 data-block-key=\"99ick\">Public Health Nurse visit</h3><p data-block-key=\"83h8u\">A nurse will call to check on feeding, development, and your recovery.</p><h3 data-block-key=\"a28tu\">Vaccinations</h3><p data-block-key=\"donb9\">These start at 2 months old.</p><p data-block-key=\"ckid1\">Appointments are arranged through your GP or HSE clinic.</p><p data-block-key=\"1nesu\"><a href=\"https://www2.hse.ie/babies-children/vaccines-your-child/\">Information on vaccines from the HSE</a>.</p>",
      "id": "ec2d1475-e108-40c7-b348-c093b14ce58b"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "value": "Employment rights",
      "id": "deb8936c-cad6-4fa8-88a3-ca7d23b1afde"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "value": "<h3 data-block-key=\"dc0ct\">Maternity leave</h3><p data-block-key=\"8l8k0\">Paid maternity leave last for 26 weeks, and you can have another 16 weeks unpaid.</p><p data-block-key=\"19kd2\">If you have enough PRSI contributions, you can claim <a href=\"https://www.gov.ie/en/department-of-social-protection/services/maternity-benefit/\">Maternity Benefit</a>.</p><h3 data-block-key=\"dq0ic\">Paternity leave</h3><p data-block-key=\"1teem\">Paternity leave lasts for 2 weeks within the first 6 months.</p><p data-block-key=\"2gvnb\">If you meet certain PRSI conditions, you can claim paid <a href=\"https://www.gov.ie/en/department-of-social-protection/services/paternity-benefit/\">Paternity Benefit</a>.</p><h3 data-block-key=\"alg88\">Parent's leave</h3><p data-block-key=\"a9tv5\">Parent's leave lasts 9 weeks per parent. This can be taken any time in the first 2 years.</p><p data-block-key=\"1vuoi\">You may be eligible for <a href=\"https://www.gov.ie/en/department-of-social-protection/services/parents-benefit/\">Parent's Benefit</a>.</p><h3 data-block-key=\"20lkl\">Parental leave (unpaid)</h3><p data-block-key=\"81lbm\">As a parent, you are entitled to up to 26 weeks per parent, per child, before your child turns 12.</p>",
      "id": "626f4b80-46ff-4c06-ba18-aad102cbc640"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "value": "Financial supports",
      "id": "d074abdc-fb80-4505-9ccf-0e881d6a7a48"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "value": "<h3 data-block-key=\"dc0ct\">Child Benefit</h3><p data-block-key=\"8a2l2\">This is a ‘universal’ payment. This means you can get it regardless of your income and PRSI record.</p><p data-block-key=\"89kr3\"><a href=\"https://www.gov.ie/en/department-of-social-protection/services/child-benefit/\">More information on Child Benefit</a>.</p><h3 data-block-key=\"11p8e\">Working Family Payment</h3><p data-block-key=\"48oct\">This is for families on low to middle incomes.</p><p data-block-key=\"3g6q0\"><a href=\"https://www.gov.ie/en/department-of-social-protection/services/working-family-payment-wfp/\">More information on the Working Family Payment</a>.</p><h3 data-block-key=\"apfqg\">Back to School Clothing and Footwear Allowance</h3><p data-block-key=\"7qquh\">This is a payment to help you meet the costs of uniforms and footwear for when your child is going to school.</p><p data-block-key=\"5q60i\"><a href=\"https://www.gov.ie/en/department-of-social-protection/services/back-to-school-clothing-and-footwear-allowance/\">More information on the Back to School Clothing and Footwear Allowance</a>.</p><h3 data-block-key=\"3sfil\">Other supports</h3><p data-block-key=\"16dk2\">Depending on family circumstances, you may be eligible for other payments such as the <a href=\"https://www.gov.ie/en/department-of-social-protection/services/one-parent-family-payment/\">One-Parent Family Payment</a> and <a href=\"https://www.gov.ie/en/department-of-social-protection/services/basic-supplementary-welfare-allowance/\">Supplementary Welfare Allowance</a>.</p>",
      "id": "f034d001-b131-4d3c-b4d7-3078508a9589"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "value": "Childcare supports",
      "id": "76594b7c-ebbe-47f7-9d71-873073ee1fb8"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "value": "<h3 data-block-key=\"dc0ct\">National Childcare Scheme (NCS)</h3><p data-block-key=\"3s8o\">The <a href=\"https://www.ncs.gov.ie/en/\">NCS</a> provides financial support to help you with early learning and childcare costs.</p><h3 data-block-key=\"bk5af\">Early Childhood Care and Education (ECCE) Scheme</h3><p data-block-key=\"1gb8t\">The <a href=\"https://www.gov.ie/en/department-of-children-disability-and-equality/publications/early-childhood-care-and-education-programme-ecce/\">ECCE Scheme</a> provides two free preschool years from age 2 years 8 months until primary school.</p><h3 data-block-key=\"cq8qe\">Local community schemes</h3><p data-block-key=\"e10gs\">Some <a href=\"https://www.gov.ie/en/department-of-children-disability-and-equality/publications/city-and-county-childcare-committees/\">councils and centres</a> provide additional supports depending on income and location.</p>",
      "id": "886068ec-add7-417a-a8e3-f174f6ef1a70"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "value": "Other practical steps",
      "id": "907998fb-b91c-4413-91fc-f1ef08cdd6f0"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "value": "<ul><li data-block-key=\"dc0ct\">add your baby to any private health insurance policy</li><li data-block-key=\"8t50\"><a href=\"https://www.ireland.ie/en/dfa/passports/how-to-apply-for-a-passport/first-child-passport/\">apply for a passport</a> if you plan to travel</li></ul>",
      "id": "e5e6fc15-a9f9-445a-a055-fcbb3e38030f"
    }
  ],
